[sliver] The 0.8 mm skirt's edge faces: the bridge is a shell segment 3.25 mm proud at the plateau and 0.8 mm at the skirt (reed-bridge/README.md, The part). The skirt is the foot of the 16 mm circumferential ramps each copper wrap rides up and over.
alternatives: A thicker skirt makes each wrap step up at the bridge's edge instead of riding onto it, lifting the copper off the wall there. Longer ramps widen the bridge's 51.4 mm arc and the copper it carries over the reeds.
