[ledge] The linter is wrong for this part's pose. The bridge prints with its outer convex face down, turned a quarter about Y (reed-bridge/README.md; trial-preparation pieces.json `small-petg`). These faces are the pocket and lead-notch ends, which look along Z in the bridge's own frame and are vertical in the print. The lint reads ledges only through an X tilt and a Z flip.
alternatives: None in the part. The lint could take a Y turn among its print poses.
